"use strict";

/* generated from story/scenes/act2_ch7.md — do not edit */

SC["c3t_open"]={img:"trials",
 t:()=>SYS(`ACT TWO — THE AZURE TRIALS`)+SYS(`CHAPTER SEVEN — THE NOTICE`)+P(`Late winter loosens its grip one drip at a time, and on the first morning the icicles let go of the kitchen eaves, a notice in vermilion ink goes up on every court's board: the <b>Azure Trials</b>, the sect's grand tournament, held once in three years. Brackets for sword, palm, and formation. A bench for the alchemists. Robes and stipends for the top sixteen.`)+P(`And at the bottom, in characters the same size as all the others, a line that stops the mountain mid-stride: <i>by charter of the founders, any soul who serves the mountain may enter.</i>`)+P(`Servants. Servants may enter.`)+P(`Bao reads it over your shoulder three times, lips moving, like a man checking a winning slip for the trick. “Top sixteen take outer-court robes. Real robes, real stipend, real cultivation manuals.” He side-eyes you. “And the steward's office clears the debts of any entrant's household that places. <i>Any</i> entrant.”`)+P(`Mei's family ledger is clean now or it isn't — but hers was never the only family, and the basement does its arithmetic out loud all morning: Tang's pot-boys counting cousins, the laundry women counting seasons of fines, Hu Lan's name traveling up and down the wash-lines like a flag. The bracket posts in five days.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Put your name on the list. In your own hand.`,go:"a2c7_clause"}]};

SC["a2c7_clause"]={t:()=>P(`It takes Bao a day and a half to find out whose hand restored the charter line, because Bao can find out anything on this mountain except how to stop looking.`)+P(`“A clerk in the rites office,” he reports, crouched by the wood-stack, voice pitched under the chopping. “Ordered to review the founding charter for the anniversary observances. Ordered by the office of—” he taps the air twice, the basement's shorthand for a name you don't say while holding kindling, “—Elder Kang.”`)+P(`A century-dead clause does not climb out of an archive by itself. Somebody went down and got it, and that somebody has been asking the stewards about you by name since midwinter. You stand in the wood-yard with the snowmelt ticking off the eaves and see the shape of it, plain as a knot in good light: the trials are a net, and the net has been sized for exactly one fish.`)+P(`The question is what to do with knowing.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Tell Mei and Bao what the net is for. They're standing in it with you.`,do:()=>{G.mei++;G.bao++;G.f.a2_told_net=true;note("Mei +1, Bao +1. Bao goes quiet for once. Mei doesn't. “Then we make the net regret it,” she says, and starts packing her bench kit that same night.");},go:"a2c7_mei"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Carry it alone. Study the net instead — every net has a mesh, and every mesh has a size.`,do:()=>{addIns(1);note("You spend two evenings working out what the trials are designed to make you show. Forewarned is forearmed; lonely is also lonely.");},go:"a2c7_mei"}]};

SC["a2c7_mei"]={t:()=>P(`The alchemists' bench is the trials' quietest bracket and its cruelest: one inner-court apprenticeship, once in three years, judged by examiners who have failed candidates for a badly tied sash. Mei has wanted it so long she's stopped saying so out loud. The herb-racks say it for her: scrubbed, ordered, ready for an examiner who hasn't asked.`)+P(`She corners you in the drying shed with her notes spread over the herb-racks like a campaign map. The remedy is half-built and it is <i>good</i> — a meridian salve that doesn't fight the channel, that follows it. You can see the missing piece from across the room, because the missing piece is yours: a thing you told her once, idly, watching her grind cloudpith — that qi-channels aren't pipes, they <i>knot</i> at the wrist and ankle, and everything the body does kinks around those knots.`)+P(`“If I build on that,” she says, not looking up, “sooner or later somebody asks me where an outer-court herb girl learned channel-knot theory that isn't in any manual on this mountain.” Now she looks up. “So I'm asking you first.”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`“Build it. It's yours — you did the work. I'll be the footnote nobody reads.”`,do:()=>{G.f.a2_mei_remedy="yes";G.mei++;note("Mei +1. She nods once, like a door closing on a decision, and grinds cloudpith until midnight.");},go:"a2c7_bao"},
  {id:"c1",l:`“Don't. Not this cycle. The wrong people are already looking at everything near me.”`,do:()=>{G.f.a2_mei_remedy="no";G.mei=Math.max(0,G.mei-1);note("Mei −1. She packs her notes away with terrible care, the way you fold a flag. “Sensible,” she says. It is the coldest word she has ever handed you.");},go:"a2c7_bao"},
  {id:"c2",l:`“Build it — and we build you a cover-theory first. Every claim re-derived from texts you could have read.”`,req:()=>(G.mind>=6),rq:"(needs Mind 6)",do:()=>{G.f.a2_mei_remedy="co";G.mei+=2;note("Mei +2. Three nights of the two of you arguing through the lattice of an alibi until her remedy has a paper trail older than your arrival. It is the most fun you have had since dying.");},go:"a2c7_bao"}]};

SC["a2c7_bao"]={t:()=>((G.f.a1_bao_debts)?(P(`Bao finds you last. He always saves the heaviest load for the end of the day. Since his bet-book burned in the Qiu scouring, his firewood debts have tripled, and the trials ring, the real one with silver in it, run out of a wine-shop two terraces down, has let him in deep on credit. He shows you the figure on a scrap of slate and then wipes it with his thumb, fast, like it burns.`)+P(`“I'm not asking you to lose,” he says, to the woodpile, to the snow, to anything but you. “I'd never — look. You <i>know</i> things. About your own matches. That's all. Knowing, ahead. That's all I'd need.”`)):(P(`Bao finds you last, grinning too wide, and the grin has arithmetic behind it. He's been running modest odds on you in the basement, copper stuff, soup-stakes, and the trials ring two terraces down, the one with actual silver in it, has noticed the only book on the mountain that prices the servant correctly. Large men with small eyes have started buying him wine he didn't order.`)+P(`“I'm not asking anything,” he says, which is how he asks. “But if a man knew how his own matches were going to go — just <i>knew</i>, ahead — a careful friend could retire his whole family from firewood.”`)))+P(`The ask hangs in the cold between you, fragile and enormous. He watches you not answer it. “Forget it,” he says finally, hoisting the carry-frame, voice bright as a cracked bell. “Train. I'll be the loud one in the stands.”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The bracket posts tomorrow. Five days were never going to be enough — so make the nights count.`,do:()=>{G.f.a2_bao_ask=true;},go:"c3t_train"}]};

SC["c3t_train"]={t:()=>P(`Five days. The whole mountain trains; the kitchens still need scrubbing, so your five days are five nights. How do you spend them?`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Bag-work and footwork with Bao behind the woodshed, until your knuckles split.`,do:()=>{addStat("body",1);G.bao++;note("Bao +1");},go:"a2c7_why"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Sit with Granny Sho and practice thread-control until the knots come without looking.`,req:()=>(G.sho>=2),rq:"(needs Granny Sho's trust)",do:()=>{addIns(2);},go:"a2c7_why"},
  {id:"c2",l:`Let Mei dose you with training tonics and tape your hands properly each dawn.`,do:()=>{addStat("heart",1);G.mei++;note("Mei +1");G.f.tonics=true;},go:"a2c7_why"},
  {id:"c3",l:`Steal into the archive's open stacks and study old trial records for patterns.`,do:()=>{addStat("mind",1);},go:"a2c7_why"}]};

SC["a2c7_why"]={t:()=>P(`The last night before the bracket posts, you climb to the wood-yard wall, where the kitchen smoke goes up in one unhurried line, and ask yourself the only question the examiners won't: why.`)+((G.f.a1_intent=="home")?(P(`Because the trials' victor is read into the sect rolls with archive rights, and somewhere in that sealed archive is every record this mountain keeps of doors, Looms, and the space between worlds. Robes are robes. You are entering a library through the roof, and the roof happens to be a tournament.`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent=="strong")?(P(`Because the ladder is real and you are done standing at the bottom of it. Every realm on this mountain was bought with something: talent, time, tribute. Yours will be bought in public, where nobody can pretend it didn't happen. Let them all watch the cripple climb.`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent=="even")?(P(`Because the charter line at the bottom of that notice is a lever, and levers only work if someone leans on them. If a servant places — places <i>honestly</i>, in front of ten thousand witnesses — then every steward who ever sold a Little Su down-mountain has to reckon with what the basement is. You are not entering a tournament. You are setting a precedent.`)):(""))+((G.f.a1_intent=="safe")?(P(`Because refusing has become more dangerous than entering. A servant who declines a restored charter right, the season after Elder Kang learned his name — that's not modesty, that's confirmation. The safest place to hide a gold thread is in a tapestry. You will enter, place respectably, and be exactly as remarkable as a clever servant and not one knot more.`)):(""))+P(`Below you the mountain is putting itself to bed: lamps going out terrace by terrace, the dragon vein humming its one silver note under the flagstones, the cloud-ring around the peak holding the last of the light like a bowl holds water. Whatever else this place is — net, ladder, ledger, trap — it is also, you have stopped pretending otherwise, beautiful.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Sleep. Tomorrow, the weather changes.`,go:"c3t_r1"}]};